        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/5e38808c13ecc929e128079b70c1642554e2a4b3" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.475ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{1}}"/></span> whose automorphism group is <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt21" id="mwNA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span>) is to transform the regular inverse Galois problem into a problem of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diophantine_geometry" title="Diophantine geometry" id="mwNQ">Diophantine geometry</a>: if (geometric) points of the moduli spaces correspond to <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt22" id="mwNg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span>-covers (or extensions of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt23" id="mwNw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\bar\\Q(T)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\bar {\mathbb {Q} }}(T)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mover>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi>
              </mrow>
              <mo stretchy="false">¯<!-- ¯ --></mo>
            </mover>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>T</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\bar {\mathbb {Q} }}(T)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/42d5fa3235fe9e70284dadca06b18a3ffa87211a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:5.254ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\bar {\mathbb {Q} }}(T)}"/></span> with Galois group <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt24" id="mwOA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span>) then it is expected that rational points are related to regular extensions of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt25" id="mwOQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\Q(T)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {Q} (T)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>T</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {Q} (T)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7ce958b3ff6841c3ceca73b1e8479a3f9a7f4633" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:5.254ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {Q} (T)}"/></span> with Galois group <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt26" id="mwOg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span>.</p>

<p id="mwOw">This geometric approach, pioneered by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_G._Thompson" title="John G. Thompson" id="mwPA">John G. Thompson</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_D._Fried" title="Michael D. Fried" id="mwPQ">Michael D. Fried</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunter_Malle" title="Gunter Malle" id="mwPg">Gunter Malle</a> and Wolfgang Matzat,<sup about="#mwt29" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-2" id="mwPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">]</span></span></a></sup> has been key to the realization of 25 of the 26 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sporadic_group" title="Sporadic group" id="mwQw">sporadic groups</a> as Galois groups over <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt30" id="mwRA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\Q"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {Q} }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {Q} }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c5909f0b54e4718fa24d5fd34d54189d24a66e9a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:1.808ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {Q} }"/></span> — the only remaining sporadic group left to realize being the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathieu_group_M23" title="Mathieu group M23" id="mwRQ">Mathieu group M23</a>.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwRg" aria-labelledby="Definitions"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Definitions">Definitions</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hurwitz_space&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Definitions"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwRw" aria-labelledby="Configuration_spaces"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Configuration_spaces">Configuration spaces</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hurwitz_space&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Configuration spaces"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwSA">Let <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt31" id="mwSQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span> be a finite group and <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt32" id="mwSg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle n}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>n</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle n}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a601995d55609f2d9f5e233e36fbe9ea26011b3b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.395ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle n}"/></span> be a fixed integer. A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Configuration_space_(mathematics)" title="Configuration space (mathematics)" id="mwSw">configuration</a> is an unordered list of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt33" id="mwTA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle n}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>n</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle n}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a601995d55609f2d9f5e233e36fbe9ea26011b3b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.395ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle n}"/></span> distincts points of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt34" id="mwTQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{A}^1(\\C)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {A} ^{1}(\mathbb {C} )}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">A</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">C</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {A} ^{1}(\mathbb {C} )}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9cba825ef2248618f5378ebfe71e10dc96727a50" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:6.22ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {A} ^{1}(\mathbb {C} )}"/></span>. Configurations form a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topological_space" title="Topological space" id="mwTg">topological space</a>: the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Configuration_space_(mathematics)" title="Configuration space (mathematics)" id="mwTw">configuration space</a> <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt35" id="mwUA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\operatorname{Conf}_n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Conf} _{n}}">
  <semantics>
