</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwmg" aria-labelledby="Hurwitz_spaces"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Hurwitz_spaces">Hurwitz spaces</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hurwitz_space&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Hurwitz spaces"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwmw">Topologically, the Hurwitz space classifying <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt91" id="mwnA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span>-covers with <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt92" id="mwnQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle n}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>n</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle n}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a601995d55609f2d9f5e233e36fbe9ea26011b3b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.395ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle n}"/></span> branch points is an unramified cover of the configuration space <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt93" id="mwng" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\operatorname{Conf}_n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Conf} _{n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>Conf</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \operatorname {Conf} _{n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/958de024ffad02dc66e622098238e757b7a4ecf0" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:6.063ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Conf} _{n}}"/></span> whose fiber above a configuration <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt94" id="mwnw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbf{t}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbf {t} }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="bold">t</mi>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbf {t} }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/16ff63cc74a931900e79b3caacbae3fa8cc66845" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.039ex; height:2.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbf {t} }"/></span> is in bijection, via the choice of a generating set of loops in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt95" id="mwoA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\pi_1(\\mathbb{P}^1 \\smallsetminus \\mathbf{t},\\, \\infty)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \pi _{1}(\mathbb {P} ^{1}\smallsetminus \mathbf {t} ,\,\infty )}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>π<!-- π --></mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>∖<!-- ∖ --></mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="bold">t</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mspace width="thinmathspace"></mspace>
        <mi mathvariant="normal">∞<!-- ∞ --></mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \pi _{1}(\mathbb {P} ^{1}\smallsetminus \mathbf {t} ,\,\infty )}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/8e9664b9d54ab3196c93f33576a167adb07ccc9f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:14.288ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \pi _{1}(\mathbb {P} ^{1}\smallsetminus \mathbf {t} ,\,\infty )}"/></span>, with the quotient <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt96" id="mwoQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"V_n/G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle V_{n}/G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>V</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mo>/</mo>
        </mrow>
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle V_{n}/G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/6fef52543596f7b92a6e6a54157565f1176c0f04" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:5.563ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle V_{n}/G}"/></span> of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt97" id="mwog" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"V_n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle V_{n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>V</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle V_{n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3ebc5a637019ce3415183f06995aeeca93547767" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.574ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle V_{n}}"/></span> by the conjugacy action of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt98" id="mwow" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"G"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle G}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>G</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle G}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f5f3c8921a3b352de45446a6789b104458c9f90b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.827ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G}"/></span>. Two points in the fiber are in the same connected component if they are represented by tuples which are in the same orbit for the action of the braid group <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt99" id="mwpA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"B_n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle B_{n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>B</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
