</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/600e80bbe00b809c8524af72ff6f20c667f862f1" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:4.931ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {H}}_{G,n}}"/></span> by a descent criterion of Weil.<sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="#cite_note-7" id="mwvQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt121" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-8" id="mwwQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwwg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwww">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxA">]</span></span></a></sup>
The scheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt122" id="mwxQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathcal{H}_{G, n}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {H}}_{G,n}}">
