</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/dbb96e056c071d13fc7702013f9273e7f5cd88a7" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:2.409ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {F} _{q}}"/></span>-points on Hurwitz spaces. This approach was highlighted by works of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Ellenberg" title="Jordan Ellenberg" id="mwAS0">Jordan Ellenberg</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akshay_Venkatesh" title="Akshay Venkatesh" id="mwAS4">Akshay Venkatesh</a>, Craig Westerland and TriThang Tran.<sup about="#mwt203" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-10" id="mwAS8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATE">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_6-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-6" id="mwATM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATU">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt207" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-11" id="mwATc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATk">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt210" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"}}'><a href="#cite_note-12" id="mwATs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAT0">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAT4">]</span></span></a></sup> Their strategy to count <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt211" id="mwAT8" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{F}_q"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {F} _{q}}">
